row(32, 25, 'MATERIAL', f'WITHOUT THE SWORD SHALL BEREAVE, AND IN THE CHAMBERS TERROR; BOTH YOUNG MAN AND VIRGIN, THE SUCKLING WITH THE MAN OF GRAY HAIRS. {HP(32, 25, (("מחוץ", "תשכל", "חרב"), "from without the sword shall bereave — \'the sword without\' ONCE in the Bible (the ink); Sifrei 342:1 (outside) quotes it"), (("ומחדרים", "אימה"), "and from the chambers terror"), (("גם", "בחור", "גם", "בתולה"), "both young man and virgin"), (("יונק", "עם", "איש", "שיבה"), "the suckling with the man of gray hair — the four ages"))} {AP(32, 25, (("מברא", "תתכל", "חרבא"), "from outside the sword shall bereave"), (("ומתוניא", "חרגת", "מותא"), "and from the chambers THE TERROR OF DEATH — the terror named death\'s"), (("אף", "עולמיהון", "אף", "עולמתהון"), "both their young men and their maidens — the possessives added"), (("ינקיהון", "עם", "אנש", "סביהון"), "their sucklings with their old men"))} Onkelos writes the meaning: the terror is death\'s, the ages are theirs. DV32-08. Fresh.')
row(32, 26, 'MATERIAL', f'I SAID: I WOULD MAKE AN END OF THEM, I WOULD MAKE THEIR MEMORY CEASE FROM AMONG MEN. {HP(32, 26, (("אמרתי", "אפאיהם"), "I said: I would scatter them (af\'eihem — a verb once in the Bible, its root disputed) — no two-token kin (the ink)"), (("אשביתה", "מאנוש", "זכרם"), "I would make their memory cease from man"))} {AP(32, 26, (("אמרית", "אחול", "רגזי", "עליהון", "ואשצנון"), "I said: I would let MY ANGER FALL upon them and destroy them — the obscure verb rendered by its consequence"), (("אבטל", "מבני", "אנשא", "דוכרניהון"), "I would abolish their memory from the sons of men"))} Onkelos writes the meaning: the unique verb given a plain sense. The compile: the decree not carried out (32:27) — a counterfactual, no ledger write. DV32-09. Fresh.')
row(32, 27, 'MATERIAL', f'WERE IT NOT THAT I DREADED THE ENEMY\'S PROVOCATION, LEST THEIR ADVERSARIES MISJUDGE, LEST THEY SAY: OUR HAND IS EXALTED AND NOT THE LORD HAS WROUGHT ALL THIS. {HP(32, 27, (("לולי", "כעס", "אויב", "אגור"), "were it not that I feared the enemy\'s provocation — the divine \'I fear\' (agur)"), (("פן", "ינכרו", "צרימו"), "lest their adversaries misjudge — \'lest\' twice in the verse, the chapter\'s two (the ink)"), (("פן", "יאמרו", "ידינו", "רמה"), "lest they say: our hand is high — 9:28\'s \'lest they say\' the song\'s kin inside the book"), (("ולא", "יהוה", "פעל", "כל", "זאת"), "and not the LORD has done all this"))} {AP(32, 27, (("אלולפון", "רגזא", "דסנאה", "כניש"), "were it not that the enemy\'s anger is GATHERED — the dread dropped from God"), (("דילמא", "יתרברב", "בעל", "דבבא"), "lest the adversary BOAST — misjudging rendered boasting"), (("ולא", "מן", "קדם", "יי", "הות", "כל", "דא"), "and not from before the LORD was all this — from before (min kodam) again"))} Onkelos writes the meaning: God does not fear; the enemy\'s anger is stored. The compile: THE ENEMY\'S BOAST the reason the decree is stayed — the argument of Exodus 32:12 and Numbers 14:16 on the tape (the kin by sense). DV32-09. Fresh.')
row(32, 28, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR THEY ARE A NATION VOID OF COUNSEL, AND THERE IS NO UNDERSTANDING IN THEM. {HP(32, 28, (("כי", "גוי", "אבד", "עצות", "המה"), "for a nation void of counsel are they — ONCE in the Bible (the ink)"), (("ואין", "בהם", "תבונה"), "and no understanding in them"))} {AP(32, 28, (("ארי", "עם", "מאבדי", "עצה", "אנון"), "for a people that DESTROYS counsel are they — void rendered destroying"), (("ולית", "בהון", "סוכלתנו"), "and no understanding in them"))} The spine (322) reads the nation as Israel and as the enemy both; Onkelos leaves it open. DV32-09. Fresh.')
row(32, 29, 'MATERIAL', f'IF THEY WERE WISE THEY WOULD UNDERSTAND THIS, THEY WOULD DISCERN THEIR LATTER END. {HP(32, 29, (("לו", "חכמו", "ישכילו", "זאת"), "had they been wise they would understand this — no two-token kin (the ink)"), (("יבינו", "לאחריתם"), "they would discern their end — 32:20\'s \'their end\' again"))} {AP(32, 29, (("אלו", "חכימו", "אסתכלו", "בדא"), "had they been wise they would have looked into this"), (("סברו", "מא", "יהי", "בסופיהון"), "they would have considered what shall be at their end"))} Onkelos word for word. DV32-10. Fresh.')
row(32, 30, 'MATERIAL', f'HOW SHOULD ONE CHASE A THOUSAND, AND TWO PUT TEN THOUSAND TO FLIGHT, EXCEPT THEIR ROCK HAD SOLD THEM AND THE LORD HAD DELIVERED THEM UP? {HP(32, 30, (("איכה", "ירדף", "אחד", "אלף"), "how should one chase a thousand — Joshua 23:10\'s kin (three shared; the Prophets\' seat cited, never read)"), (("ושנים", "יניסו", "רבבה"), "and two put ten thousand to flight — THE PARSER\'S JOINED THOUSAND: the verse read as [1, 1002] with \'one\' marked, the thousand and the two joined and the ten thousand not counted (the compile\'s second guard, 20b)"), (("אם", "לא", "כי", "צורם", "מכרם"), "except that their Rock had sold them — the Rock the fifth of eight"), (("ויהוה", "הסגירם"), "and the LORD had delivered them up — the Name with vav, its one such seat in the chapter (the ink)"))} {AP(32, 30, (("אכדין", "ירדוף", "חד", "אלפא"), "how shall one chase a thousand"), (("ותרין", "יערקון", "לרבותא"), "and two make a myriad flee"), (("תקיפהון", "מסרנון", "ויי", "אשלמנון"), "their Mighty One handed them over and the LORD delivered them — the Rock the Mighty One; the export carries a parenthesized variant \'for\' before it, not cut"))} THE EXPORT\'S VARIANT (a bracketed \'ari\' — \'for\' — before the Mighty One, the two readings side by side) noted, never counted. The compile: the two numbers the parser reads here are not a count in the world (a proverb) — guarded, no ledger write. DV32-10. Fresh.')
row(32, 31, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR THEIR ROCK IS NOT AS OUR ROCK, AND OUR ENEMIES ARE JUDGES. {HP(32, 31, (("כי", "לא", "כצורנו", "צורם"), "for not as our Rock is their rock — the rock twice in the verse, the sixth and seventh of eight (the ink); no two-token kin"), (("ואיבינו", "פלילים"), "and our enemies are judges (pelilim) — the word of Exodus 21:22"))} {AP(32, 31, (("ארי", "לא", "כתקפנא", "תקפהון"), "for not as our Strength is their strength — the two rocks the two strengths"), (("ובעלי", "דבבנא", "הוו", "דיננא"), "and our enemies HAVE BECOME OUR JUDGES — the judges given a verb"))} Onkelos word for word in sense. DV32-10. Fresh.')
row(32, 32, 'MATERIAL', f'FOR THEIR VINE IS OF THE VINE OF SODOM AND OF THE FIELDS OF GOMORRAH; THEIR GRAPES ARE GRAPES OF GALL, THEIR CLUSTERS ARE BITTER. {HP(32, 32, (("כי", "מגפן", "סדם", "גפנם"), "for of the vine of Sodom is their vine — Sodom and Gomorrah named (29:22\'s four cities on the tape)"), (("ומשדמת", "עמרה"), "and of the fields of Gomorrah"), (("ענבמו", "ענבי", "רוש"), "their grapes grapes of gall (rosh)"), (("אשכלת", "מררת", "למו"), "clusters of bitterness to them"))} {AP(32, 32, (("ארי", "כפרענות", "עמא", "דסדום", "פרענותהון"), "for like THE PUNISHMENT of the people of Sodom is their punishment — the vine rendered the retribution"), (("מחתהון", "בישין", "כרישי", "חוין"), "their blows are evil like the heads of serpents — the gall rendered the serpents\' heads"), (("ותשלמת", "עובדיהון", "כמררותהון"), "and the requital of their deeds like their bitterness"))} Onkelos writes the meaning: the botany is a sentence — Sodom\'s punishment for Sodom\'s deeds (the tape\'s own entry, Genesis 19). DV32-10. Fresh.')
row(32, 33, 'MATERIAL', f'THEIR WINE IS THE VENOM OF SERPENTS AND THE CRUEL POISON OF ASPS. {HP(32, 33, (("חמת", "תנינם", "יינם"), "the venom of serpents is their wine — no two-token kin (the ink)"), (("וראש", "פתנים", "אכזר"), "and the cruel gall of asps — \'the venom of asps\' with Job 20:16 alone in this form (the ink)"))} {AP(32, 33, (("הא", "כמרת", "תניניא", "כס", "פרענותהון"), "behold, like the gall of serpents is THE CUP OF THEIR PUNISHMENT — the wine rendered the cup of retribution"), (("וכריש", "פתני", "חוין", "אכזראין"), "and like the head of cruel asp-serpents"))} Onkelos writes the meaning: the wine a cup of punishment (with 32:32). DV32-10. Fresh.')
row(32, 34, 'MATERIAL', f'IS NOT THIS LAID UP IN STORE WITH ME, SEALED UP IN MY TREASURIES? {HP(32, 34, (("הלא", "הוא", "כמס", "עמדי"), "is it not stored up with Me — no two-token kin (the ink)"), (("חתם", "באוצרתי"), "sealed in My treasuries"))} {AP(32, 34, (("הלא", "כל", "עובדיהון", "גלן", "קדמי"), "are not all their deeds REVEALED BEFORE ME — the stored thing named as their deeds"), (("גניזין", "ליום", "דינא", "באוצרי"), "hidden away FOR THE DAY OF JUDGMENT in My treasury — the day named"))} Onkelos writes the meaning: the treasuries hold the deeds against judgment day (the translator\'s second eschatology, with 32:12). DV32-11. Fresh.')
